We will partially migrate to AWS London region, with Ireland region as a backup if the London cloud fails.
Will use a hybrid cloud to keep high security for customer information while keeping the application fast and scalable

Use Amazon CloudFront for handling API requests with AWS Shield Advanced to ensure maximum protection against DDoS attacks

Amazon Cognito used for customer sign in and sign up to ensure proper authentication

AWS is compliant with Payment Card Industry Security Standards and the ISO/IEC 27001 (security management standard that specifies best practices and security controls) - this keeps our application secure and up to date with modern best practices

Would use AWS Direct Connect to connect our private to public - this gives us a dedicated private link to AWS to improve security by ensuring we aren't transmitting sensitive information across the public internet

Amazon CloudWatch to keep an eye on application health and system performance
AWS CloudTrail for tracking and auditing user activity
Both improve overall application security